<title>USA: Disney near pact to buy Mammoth records-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Disney near pact to buy Mammoth records-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Walt Disney Co is close to signing a $20 million to $25 million pact to buy the Mammoth Records independent record label, a deal that could initiate a reorganization of Disney's struggling pop music business, The Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Monday's electronic edition, the paper said Mammoth owner Jay Faires is weighing a competing offer from Polygram NV's A&amp;M Records.</p>
<p>The paper said the information came from &quot;people familiar with the situation.&quot;</p>
<p>Disney and Mammoth declined to comment for the story.</p>
</text>
